From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:14:02 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: a text-only MCP bridge for models that take no
 images; results compact and capped

An agent on an OpenAI-compatible provider (OpenCode with a corporate
model) failed every turn after a screenshot with HTTP 400 "Failed to read
HTTP message": the client puts the screenshot into the conversation (as a
user message with image/content parts) and that endpoint refuses it.
- `Meridian --mcp-bridge --text-only` (or MERIDIAN_MCP_TEXT_ONLY=1): the
  screenshot tool isn't listed, and a screenshot asked for anyway answers
  with text pointing at read_page and get_interactive_elements.
- Tool results are compact JSON (pretty printing was a third of a long
  element list) and cut at 100 KB on a whole UTF-8 character, with a note
  on how to ask for less (agent/mcp_result.h, unit-tested).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
